 {"id":"QA-SPECLANG-5-R6","status":"complete","priority":"P3","type":"bug","complexity":2,"title":"P3 \u2014 two corruption-guard bypasses named by judge 1c52e0d4: 'mcp status' exits 0 on a corrupt DB, and a stale compiled controller.js still calls new Database()","reasoning":"Both were reported as uncovered failure paths in the tier-2 verdict for QA-SPECLANG-5-R2 (run 1c52e0d4, code land a283b41e). (0) speclang mcp status (bin/speclang:1414) reads pid/status files only and never opens the state DB, so a corrupt .speclang/speclang.db reports 'Status: Not running' with exit 0 - a silent lie of the same class QA-SPECLANG-5 fixed one layer down. (1) specs/implementation.spec.dir/src/controller.js:34 is a stale COMPILED artifact that still constructs new Database(...); if TS resolution ever falls back to the .js sibling, the guard is bypassed silently.","acceptance_criteria":"(0) With 4KB of random bytes at .speclang/speclang.db, speclang mcp status either exits non-zero with the CorruptStateDatabaseError diagnostic or explicitly reports the DB unreadable - it must never report a confident 'Not running'. (1) grep -R for the direct Database constructor over specs/**/controller.{ts,js} returns only the guarded helper, or the stale .js artifact is regenerated/removed and a test pins that the .js and .ts copies agree. Tests cover both.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"f3c9fd10af92a33e0b0eabd68c6d3700b7d25cb647fbd8805b4c61e304b2842c","evidence":[{"run_id":"c62e9f0a","ts":"2026-11-17T11:20:55.599691+00:00"}]},"capability_tags":[],"created_at":"2026-11-17T08:23:56.482783+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T11:20:55.599691+00:00","foreman_note":"CAP lesson (2026-11-17): a compound criterion (4 clauses in one string) cannot be graded inside the judge's 100-iteration cap. Split acceptance into atomic criteria, one behaviour each, with the proof commands inside the criterion text.","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/speclang-QA-SPECLANG-5-R6","branch":"wt/QA-SPECLANG-5-R6","sessi