 {"id":"UX-004-R1","status":"complete","priority":"P4","type":"bug","complexity":3,"title":"P4 — SUPPORT.md:15 advertises GitHub Discussions, which is not enabled on the repo (dead support channel)","reasoning":"Found by the gitreins tier-2 judge for UX-004 (verdict 1d25bff7) and re-verified by the foreman at HEAD on 2026-11-17:\n  SUPPORT.md:15  - **Discussions:** [GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/dexdat/SpecLang/discussions)\n  gh api repos/dexdat/SpecLang --jq '{has_discussions, has_issues}' -> {\"archived\":false,\"has_discussions\":false,\"has_issues\":true}\n  The same tick's new .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml:5-8 states in a comment that GitHub Discussions is NOT enabled, so the tree now contradicts itself: the issue-template chooser routes users to the issue tracker while SUPPORT.md still sends them to a Discussions page that does not exist for this repo. A stranger following SUPPORT.md reaches a dead channel.\n  Doc-severity P4 per the doc-lane ruling (policy cap, not a new assessment of the finding).\n  FIX: either remove the Discussions bullet from SUPPORT.md and name the issue tracker as the single support channel (matching config.yml), or enable Discussions and link it. Do not invent a third channel.","acceptance_criteria":"From the repo root: (1) SUPPORT.md no longer lists a Discussions channel that does not exist — `grep -ci discussions SUPPORT.md` prints 0, OR the bullet is replaced by a link to a channel that is actually enabled and `gh api repos/dexdat/SpecLang --jq .has_discussions` prints true when the bullet is kept; (2) whichever state is chosen, .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml and SUPPORT.md agree — the channel named in one is named in the other and no file claims Discussions is disabled while another advertises it (`grep -rn -i discussions SUPPORT.md .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml` read side by side); (3) the remaining support links resolve (gh api for the repo's has_issues=true). Evidence: the greps and the gh api output pasted